1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,333
You rank number one on Google. But when a buyer asks ChatGPT, your competitor gets named instead.

2
00:00:08,533 --> 00:00:12,907
This may happen more often than most founders expect.

3
00:00:13,107 --> 00:00:20,050
Today: what AI SEO actually changes, and what stays the same, for Indian brands.

4
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:23,280
First, the basic difference.

5
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:30,949
Classic SEO is about ranking. Your page sits at a position on a list of ten blue links.

6
00:00:31,149 --> 00:00:38,907
AI search is about being mentioned. The tool writes one answer and names a few brands inside it.

7
00:00:39,107 --> 00:00:48,473
On Google, position five still gets some clicks. In an AI answer, if you are not named, the buyer may never see you.

8
00:00:48,673 --> 00:00:54,247
Now the good news. A lot of what you already do still counts.

9
00:00:54,447 --> 00:01:03,501
One. Your pages must be easy to crawl. If search bots cannot read your site, nothing else matters.

10
00:01:03,701 --> 00:01:12,227
Google says its AI features use the same core SEO practices as normal search, with no special extra markup.

11
00:01:12,427 --> 00:01:21,985
Two. Clear, helpful content still wins. Pages that answer real questions directly are easier to quote.

12
00:01:22,185 --> 00:01:31,503
Three. Reputation still matters. Reviews, press and links from trusted sites build trust in both worlds.

13
00:01:31,703 --> 00:01:37,277
Now, what actually changes. There are four big shifts.

14
00:01:37,477 --> 00:01:47,923
Change one. Questions get longer. Buyers type full questions, like best sunscreen for oily skin under 500 rupees.

15
00:01:48,123 --> 00:01:56,025
In India, many of these questions mix Hindi and English. Test the way your buyers actually speak.

16
00:01:56,225 --> 00:02:06,719
Change two. Other websites speak for you. AI answers often lean on reviews, lists, marketplaces and forums.

17
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:12,902
So mentions on the right third party sites may matter as much as your own homepage.

18
00:02:13,102 --> 00:02:21,988
Change three. Answers change between runs. The same question can name different brands on different days.

19
00:02:22,188 --> 00:02:28,314
So you track how often you appear across many runs, not one fixed position.

20
00:02:28,514 --> 00:02:40,088
Change four. Every platform behaves differently. ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity and Google AI Mode can all give different answers.

21
00:02:40,288 --> 00:02:45,574
Being strong on one platform does not mean you show up on the others.

22
00:02:45,774 --> 00:02:49,236
So what can an Indian brand do this month?

23
00:02:49,436 --> 00:02:55,922
Keep your SEO basics strong. Do not pause what already works on Google.

24
00:02:56,122 --> 00:03:03,568
Write ten real buyer questions, including a few in Hinglish, and test them on three AI tools.

25
00:03:03,768 --> 00:03:10,734
Note which websites are listed as sources. Those are the places to earn a mention.

26
00:03:10,933 --> 00:03:17,348
Add a clear FAQ to your key pages, answering those exact questions in plain words.

27
00:03:17,548 --> 00:03:22,210
Then repeat the same questions next month, and compare.

28
00:03:22,409 --> 00:03:28,272
Doing this across five AI platforms by hand can take hours every month.

29
00:03:28,472 --> 00:03:36,950
Jeevan AI runs your buyer questions on ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity, Claude and Google AI Mode for you.

30
00:03:37,150 --> 00:03:43,708
You see your visibility on each platform side by side, so the gaps are easy to spot.

31
00:03:43,908 --> 00:03:48,858
You see which competitors get named when you don't, and how often.

32
00:03:49,058 --> 00:03:55,976
And you see every website the AI tools listed as a source, so your outreach list is ready.

33
00:03:56,176 --> 00:04:03,070
Next episode: how to rank in AI search, with patterns we saw in tested queries.

34
00:04:03,270 --> 00:04:11,676
Comment one question your buyers ask, and we may test it in a future episode. Subscribe for the full series.
